        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A methanolic solution of pivalic acid (L1H; 51.06 mg, 0.5 mmol in 5 mL) was deprotonated with triethylamine (139.5 μL, 1 mmol), then solid 2,6-dimethoxyphenol (L′H; 77.08 mg, 0.5 mmol) was slowly added while sonicating. The solution was diluted with MeOH/MeCN (9 mL/10 mL), followed by addition of 1 mL of methanolic dysprosium nitrate hydrate (136.98 mg, 0.3 mmol). The mixture was left undisturbed at room temperature; colorless crystals of 1 suitable for SCXRD formed after slow evaporation of MeOH/MeCN for 3 d.",
